    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0193" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to King Farouk of
                        Egypt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d149-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tunis</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-20">20 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On landing in French North Africa I have just heard of your motor
                        accident.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d149-f2"/> I am deeply sorry and hope to see
                    you when I am in Egypt.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D.
                    Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d149-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d149-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the Advanced Liaison Group, Allied Force Headquarters, North Africa, to
                    the Headquarters, United States Army Forces in the Middle East, Cairo, as
                    message 952, which was marked as being from Roosevelt, for the eyes of Kirk
                    alone, and began “Please deliver the following to His Majesty the King”. Kirk
                    forwarded the message to the King via Hassanayn on November 21, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d149-f2" n="2" xml:id="d149-f2-content">
                <p>See Hull’s telegram of November 18, 1943, to Roosevelt, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg97">p. 97</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
